class Solution {
    public List<List<Integer>> minimumAbsDifference(int[] arr) {
        Arrays.sort(arr);
        List<List<Integer>> anss=new ArrayList<>();
        int minDiff=Integer.MAX_VALUE;
        for(int i=1;i<arr.length;i++){
            minDiff=Math.min(minDiff, arr[i]-arr[i-1]);
        }
        for(int i=1;i<arr.length;i++){
            if(arr[i]-arr[i-1]==minDiff){
                anss.add(Arrays.asList(arr[i-1],arr[i]));
            }
        }
        return anss;
    }
}
Explantion:
First, sort the array so that elements with the smallest differences become adjacent.
Traverse the sorted array once to find the minimum absolute difference between neighboring elements.
Traverse again and collect all adjacent pairs whose difference equals the minimum difference.
Return the list of these pairs as the final answer.
